From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Boris Krasnovskiy <boris.krasnovskiy@ezurio.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] usb: common: usb-conn-gpio: reassert role unconditionally on
 resume

dwc3 (this board runs it in OTG dr_mode) reconnects on its own system
resume using whatever role it had before suspend, without consulting
this connector at all -- dwc3_set_mode()/__dwc3_set_mode() never dedup
a role-switch call at that level, since the controller's
current_dr_role stays OTG.

usb_conn_resume() re-read the ID/VBUS GPIOs after resuming, but
usb_conn_detect_cable()'s "repeated role" dedup then swallowed the
call to usb_role_switch_set_role() whenever the resolved role matched
the last one -- which is the common case across a suspend/resume
cycle. So dwc3 was left standing on its own premature, blind
reconnect, and nothing ever told it to redo that reconnect against the
now-confirmed-stable CC/ID state, leading to unreliable reconnection
after resume.

Fix it by marking the resume-triggered detection the same way the
driver already marks its initial post-probe detection: both are cases
where the role must be (re-)applied even if it happens to match
info->last_role, since in neither case has this driver actually told
the role switch about it yet for the current system state.

Signed-off-by: Boris Krasnovskiy <boris.krasnovskiy@ezurio.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/usb/common/usb-conn-gpio.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/drivers/usb/common/usb-conn-gpio.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/common/usb-conn-gpio.c
@@ -344,6 +344,7 @@ static int __maybe_unused usb_conn_resume(struct device *dev)
 	if (info->vbus_gpiod)
 		enable_irq(info->vbus_irq);
 
+	info->initial_detection = true;
 	usb_conn_queue_dwork(info, 0);
 
 	return 0;
